    },
    {
      "id": "th-1017-2",
      "at": "2026-10-17T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Which one is you?\n\n1. You train when no fight is booked\n2. You keep going after getting dropped in sparring\n3. You've never needed a crowd to show up\n\nDrop the number.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "fighter-without-a-record",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-17T16:37:00Z",
      "thread_id": "18138306568650982",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DemjYjCkTKi"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1017-3",
      "at": "2026-10-17T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "The sparring session you lose to someone better is worth more than ten you win.\n\nGetting picked apart shows you every hole at once.\n\nWatch it back the same night. Every mistake is right there.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "mindset-without-a-fight",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-17T21:35:57Z",
      "thread_id": "18354364960302026",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DenFmcnlBk6"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1018-1",
      "at": "2026-10-18T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "You're mentally tougher than you think if you've lost and come back the next day.\n\nNot the next week. The next day.\n\nThat's the whole test.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "mentally-tougher",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T11:35:57Z",
      "thread_id": "18209333827371523",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Deoluj3oPR9"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1018-2",
      "at": "2026-10-18T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "What do you say in your head when you get hit clean?\n\nOne word beats a speech. Something like: reset.\n\nWhat's yours?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "calm-without-experience",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T16:36:55Z",
      "thread_id": "18638510098018208",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DepILAhmkse"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1018-3",
      "at": "2026-10-18T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "chain",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "How to stay calm in a fight when you don't have years of experience. A thread.",
      "chain": [
        "1. Exhale on every punch.\nYou can't panic and breathe at the same time.",
        "2. One job per round.\nJust the jab. Just the feet. A quiet head moves faster.",
        "3. Expect to get hit.\nIt's information, not failure. The shock goes away.",
        "4. Calm feet, calm head.\nWhen it gets chaotic, slow your feet first. The rest follows."
      ],
      "from": "calm-without-experience",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T21:36:49Z",
      "thread_id": "18023331710945637",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DepqZXNlcR9"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1019-1",
      "at": "2026-10-19T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "A bad session ruining your whole day isn't weakness.\n\nIt means you care more than most people in the gym.\n\nJust don't let it ruin tomorrow's session too.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "made-for-combat-sports",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T11:36:02Z",
      "thread_id": "18146666725600741",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DerKiJ9mxbT"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1019-2",
      "at": "2026-10-19T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Rest days.\n\nDo they feel like recovery or like punishment?\n\nBe honest.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "made-for-combat-sports",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T16:40:37Z",
      "thread_id": "18097164527662048",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DertY5aFDoh"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1019-3",
      "at": "2026-10-19T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "You don't need weights to hit harder.\n\nTurn the back foot. Relax until impact. Exhale sharp on every shot.\n\nPower starts on the floor. No pivot, no punch.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "power-without-weights",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T21:36:06Z",
      "thread_id": "18111799088183306",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DesPM4LgV6K"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1020-1",
      "at": "2026-10-20T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "The hardest punch isn't the strongest one.\n\nIt's the one they walk into.\n\nTiming beats strength every time.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "power-without-weights",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-20T11:36:02Z",
      "thread_id": "18115162027838143",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DetvU1_oOqc"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1020-2",
      "at": "2026-10-20T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Training alone this week?\n\nWhat's your go-to solo session?\n\nShadowboxing, bag rounds, footwork, or tape study?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "dangerous-without-a-partner",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-20T16:32:14Z",
      "thread_id": "18107458187523064",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DeuRN-_kc_q"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1020-3",
      "at": "2026-10-20T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "No partner? Give every bag round a rule.\n\nOnly counters this round. Only body shots the next.\n\nYou build reactions, not just punches.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "dangerous-without-a-partner",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-20T21:36:07Z",
      "thread_id": "18411428233094157",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Deu0ACBAZ4l"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1021-1",
      "at": "2026-10-21T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Fear before a fight isn't the problem.\n\nFeel it. Name it. Walk out anyway.\n\nThat's the entire skill.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "go-anyway",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-21T11:36:01Z",
      "thread_id": "17940524586385988",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DewUHv9FLr_"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1021-2",
      "at": "2026-10-21T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Started combat sports late?\n\nHow old were you when you walked into your first gym?\n\nCurious how many of you are out there.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "started-late",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-21T16:32:59Z",
      "thread_id": "18100925747630241",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Dew2GqOlTdO"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1021-3",
      "at": "2026-10-21T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "When training suddenly feels harder, most people think they're getting worse.\n\nUsually it's the opposite.\n\nYou're starting to notice mistakes you couldn't see before. That's what leveling up feels like from the inside.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "about-to-level-up",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-21T21:36:01Z",
      "thread_id": "18132443602748373",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DexYyMikqip"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1022-1",
      "at": "2026-10-22T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Stop caring how it looks.\n\nStart caring if it works.\n\nThat switch is when you actually start getting good.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "about-to-level-up",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-22T11:35:59Z",
      "thread_id": "18095202590244313",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Dey46bsFUEY"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1022-2",
      "at": "2026-10-22T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Which one is you?\n\n1. Training feels harder, not easier\n2. The guys who used to beat you are struggling now\n3. Sparring feels slower than it used to\n\nDrop the number.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "about-to-level-up",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-22T16:41:03Z",
      "thread_id": "17918300100464331",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Dezb0zhlAFO"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1022-3",
      "at": "2026-10-22T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Started late? Ask more questions than anyone in the gym.\n\nOne question a session to the best person there.\n\nMost will help. Nobody's ever annoyed by someone who wants to learn.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "started-late",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-22T21:36:02Z",
      "thread_id": "18104869901266042",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Dez9lIHEu_R"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1023-1",
      "at": "2026-10-23T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Hard sparring every week makes most beginners worse, not tougher.\n\nYou learn to survive, not to fight. Light rounds with one rule teach more than a war you just get through.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-23T11:36:06Z",
      "thread_id": "18115334075011347",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De1dtnxkQBd"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1023-2",
      "at": "2026-10-23T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Cardio, hands or head: which one goes first for you in round three?\n\nPick one. Then say what you do when it goes.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-23T16:32:41Z",
      "thread_id": "18135756361671839",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De1_qcnGqKS"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1023-3",
      "at": "2026-10-23T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "I had a ruptured appendix the day before a fight.\n\nThat's the closest I've come to quitting. What kept me in it wasn't a plan. It was \"I can't give up.\"\n\nNot smart advice. Just the honest answer.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "founder",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-23T21:36:04Z",
      "thread_id": "18636690688057466",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De2iYT8gTlD"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1024-1",
      "at": "2026-10-24T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Shadowboxing without a target is cardio with your hands up.\n\nPick an opponent. Give him a lefty stance and a habit of dropping his right. Then fight him for three rounds.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-24T11:36:00Z",
      "thread_id": "17937995562394435",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De4CgMqlWkX"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1024-2",
      "at": "2026-10-24T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "What did your first coach get wrong?\n\nOr what did they get right that you only understood a year later?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-24T16:32:33Z",
      "thread_id": "18439235605197095",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De4kcQhlHsD"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1024-3",
      "at": "2026-10-24T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Slept five hours? Do technique rounds today, not hard ones.\n\nTired sparring teaches bad habits and gets people hurt. Save the war for a day you can actually think.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "missed",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1025-1",
      "at": "2026-10-25T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Comparing yourself to the guy a year ahead is how people quit.\n\nHe's already made a year of mistakes you haven't. Compare yourself to you in March.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-25T11:36:48Z",
      "thread_id": "17914318209497626",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De6nY9VkfhK"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1025-2",
      "at": "2026-10-25T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "What do you still do from month one, even though you know it's wrong?\n\nCommon one: dropping the back hand after the jab.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-25T16:41:11Z",
      "thread_id": "18199356481380623",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De7KOiClpMe"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1025-3",
      "at": "2026-10-25T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "chain",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Your jab feels weak? Check these five things before you blame your arm.",
      "chain": [
        "1. Elbow.\nIf it flares out, the punch loses its straight line. Keep it pointing at the floor until the arm extends.",
        "2. Shoulder.\nRotate it up toward your chin at the end. Free reach, and it covers your jaw.",
        "3. Return.\nA jab that stays out is a push. Fire it and bring it back at the same speed.",
        "4. Feet.\nIf you step and then punch, the jab lands half a beat late. Move together.",
        "5. Breath.\nExhale on contact. Holding your breath makes the arm stiff."
      ],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-25T21:37:00Z",
      "thread_id": "18107036273252094",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De7r-HrkjS7"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1026-1",
      "at": "2026-10-26T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "I tore a knee ligament in a street fight.\n\nI took a guy down like a BJJ guy, on pavement. The mat has rules. Pavement doesn't. Training for a sport and training for the street are two different jobs.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "founder",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-26T11:35:57Z",
      "thread_id": "17908719879664073",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De9MFu0FmX6"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1026-2",
      "at": "2026-10-26T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Hard sparring or ten rounds on the pads: which leaves you more sore?\n\nAnd which one made you better?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-26T16:41:11Z",
      "thread_id": "18027847484696527",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De9vBDGoLaW"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1026-3",
      "at": "2026-10-26T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Three minutes of arm circles isn't a warm up.\n\nSkip rope until you sweat, then shadowbox at half speed for two rounds. Your first hard breath shouldn't come in your first real round.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-26T21:36:15Z",
      "thread_id": "18139364512711604",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De-QyGBH6EW"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1027-1",
      "at": "2026-10-27T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Try the new move in sparring. Even if you lose the round.\n\nWinning with your best three tricks teaches you nothing. Failing with a new one shows you what to fix.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-27T11:36:02Z",
      "thread_id": "18038501180896977",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/De_w5OWG9hV"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1027-2",
      "at": "2026-10-27T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Music in the gym or no music?\n\nSome people can't think with it. Some can't start without it. Which one are you?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-27T16:41:28Z",
      "thread_id": "18127306924839913",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DfAT2RplMM6"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1027-3",
      "at": "2026-10-27T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "My first Muay Thai fight was a draw.\n\nI hit him with a right hand while the ref was separating us. He went down. It was not clean at all.\n\nOfficial result: a draw. The scorecard doesn't care what you remember.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "founder",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-27T21:36:05Z",
      "thread_id": "18170030296478641",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DfA1j4Cj9oh"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1028-1",
      "at": "2026-10-28T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Rest isn't lazy.\n\nSkipping it is how you end up with a six week injury. Sleep, eat real food, take the day off. The boring half of training is the half that holds the rest together.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-28T11:36:02Z",
      "thread_id": "18104963645455353",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DfCVr9IkRkL"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1028-2",
      "at": "2026-10-28T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Boxing or Muay Thai for a total beginner?\n\nSkip \"whichever your gym teaches\". Pick one and give me the reason.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-28T16:41:29Z",
      "thread_id": "18000975144012531",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DfC4o7biRLj"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1028-3",
      "at": "2026-10-28T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Stuck on a plateau? Change the rule, not the effort.\n\nSpar a round using only your jab. Or fight a round going backward. You'll find the gaps your usual game hides.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1029-1",
      "at": "2026-10-29T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Being scared of getting hit doesn't make you a bad fighter.\n\nIt makes you honest. The ones who claim they don't care usually haven't been hit properly yet.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1029-2",
      "at": "2026-10-29T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "How long until you stopped closing your eyes when something came at your face?\n\nFirst week, first month, or still working on it?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1029-3",
      "at": "2026-10-29T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Training in the morning? A banana and a glass of water is enough.\n\nSkip the big breakfast you can't hold down in round three. Eat the real meal after.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1030-1",
      "at": "2026-10-30T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "The first body shot isn't the painful part.\n\nIt's the second where you realise you can't breathe and still have two minutes left.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1030-2",
      "at": "2026-10-30T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Where do you feel it first when you're gassed?\n\nLegs, lungs or arms?\n\nAnd what do you do about it?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1030-3",
      "at": "2026-10-30T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Cutting a little weight?\n\nLose it from water and food in the last 3 days, not by skipping meals all month.\n\nStarving in camp means you show up to sparring with nothing to give.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1031-1",
      "at": "2026-10-31T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Bad at defence? Spar a round where you're not allowed to punch.\n\nOnly slip, block and move. You'll find out fast which punch you always see too late.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1031-2",
      "at": "2026-10-31T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Lost a round to a smaller guy?\n\nBest thing that can happen to your ego. Better in the gym than in front of a crowd.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1031-3",
      "at": "2026-10-31T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "I tore a knee ligament in a street fight and broke my fibula a while later.\n\nBoth times the training stopped and I had to find something else to do with my head.\n\nSo I learned to code.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "founder",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1101-1",
      "at": "2026-11-01T12:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "What do you still do from month one, even though you know it's wrong?\n\nStaring at the gloves instead of the chest is a classic. What's yours?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1101-2",
      "at": "2026-11-01T17:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Shadowboxing in front of a mirror is mostly vanity.\n\nTurn the mirror off and close your eyes for one round. Your feet will tell you the truth.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1101-3",
      "at": "2026-11-01T22:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Sore shins from kicking? Don't stop hitting the bag.\n\nStart with half power and add a little each week. Skin and bone adapt to what you ask of them, slowly.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1102-1",
      "at": "2026-11-02T12:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Being nervous the night before is normal.\n\nBeing the person who goes to bed anyway is the skill.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1102-2",
      "at": "2026-11-02T17:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Gym or home training for a beginner?\n\nPick one and say why. The answer changes more than people admit.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1102-3",
      "at": "2026-11-02T22:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Hands drop when you're tired. Fix it before you're tired.\n\nDo your last bag round with a rule: every punch ends with the hand back at the chin. Slow is fine.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1103-1",
      "at": "2026-11-03T12:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Hard session tonight?\n\nEat a real meal 3 hours before, not 30 minutes.\n\nOtherwise your stomach is doing round one without you.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1103-2",
      "at": "2026-11-03T17:30:00Z",
      "kind": "chain",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Five things that go through your head before your first sparring session.\n\nDoes it sound like you?",
      "chain": [
        "1. The urge to explain yourself.\nYou'll want to say you're new before the round starts. Don't. Nobody cares and it makes you smaller.",
        "2. The one thing you don't want to happen.\nUsually it's getting hit in the face. It will happen in the first minute and the world carries on.",
        "3. The feeling that everyone is watching.\nThey're thinking about their own round.",
        "4. Your breathing going shallow.\nExhale out loud on the first punch. It resets your head.",
        "5. A strange calm after the first clean hit.\nAfter that you're just doing the work."
      ],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1103-3",
      "at": "2026-11-03T22:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Feedback right after the round, or the next day?\n\nMost people say next day. Then they wish they'd asked straight away.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1104-1",
      "at": "2026-11-04T12:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "A good jab beats a fancy combination.\n\nIf you can't land one clean straight punch against a moving partner, the three-punch combo is just noise.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1104-2",
      "at": "2026-11-04T17:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Who got you into this?\n\nA friend, a movie, a bully, an older brother. Last one's my guess for half of you.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1104-3",
      "at": "2026-11-04T22:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "I've trained in Zurich, Essaouira, Sao Paulo and Koh Samui.\n\nThe warm up is the same everywhere. What changes is who stays serious when the coach looks away.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "founder",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1105-1",
      "at": "2026-11-05T12:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Trash talk before a fight is for the crowd.\n\nThe fighter who needs to talk is usually the one doing the convincing.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1105-2",
      "at": "2026-11-05T17:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Sparring tomorrow? Cut your nails, wash your mouthguard and pack the bag tonight.\n\nOne less thing to think about means one less thing that goes wrong.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1105-3",
      "at": "2026-11-05T22:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Best conditioning of your life, or best technique?\n\nPick one. Then say what you'd lose first.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-25T17:10:40Z)"
    }
  ]
}
